WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.792
Run this query and focus on rows with the same salary.

00:00:03.792 --> 00:00:06.922
ROW_NUMBER still gives them different sequence numbers.

00:00:06.922 --> 00:00:09.752
RANK gives them the same rank and leaves a gap.

00:00:09.752 --> 00:00:13.137
DENSE_RANK gives the same rank but no gap.

00:00:13.137 --> 00:00:17.382
This side-by-side comparison makes the business differences visible.

00:00:17.382 --> 00:00:21.052
Ranking functions differ mainly in how they handle ties.

00:00:21.052 --> 00:00:27.332
ROW_NUMBER forces a unique sequence, RANK leaves gaps after ties, and DENSE_RANK does not.

00:00:27.332 --> 00:00:31.187
Add deterministic tie-breakers when a unique order matters;

00:00:31.187 --> 00:00:35.120
otherwise two executions can choose different rows among tied values.
